                <pb facs="0387" n="279" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.1115 Wright, Lucy: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Chefoo</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Webber</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chefoo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-04-05T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 5, 1927—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 6—10:30
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>In reply to Department’s telegram April 4, 6 p.m.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d296-f1"
                    /> Miss Lucy Wright and other missionaries Baptist Hospital, Hwanghsien, now
                    safe and well in Chefoo. In view of the uncertainty of conditions, possible
                    break-down communications motor roadway, Chefoo, Weihsien, and recommendation
                    made by Chinese authorities, all women and children and practically all left in
                    the district have come to Chefoo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Webber</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
